WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.278 --> 00:00:04.122
Before comparing options, make the decision and its boundaries

2
00:00:04.144 --> 00:00:07.522
clear. What is being considered? What needs to stay

3
00:00:07.544 --> 00:00:10.633
in place? Who can recommend a change, who reviews

4
00:00:10.656 --> 00:00:13.722
it, and who can approve it? Those questions protect

5
00:00:13.744 --> 00:00:16.878
good ideas from being mistaken for decisions already made.

6
00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:20.689
In our continuing example, a team is considering how

7
00:00:20.711 --> 00:00:23.756
to send appointment reminders. The team has not decided

8
00:00:23.778 --> 00:00:26.933
to remove mail. Its task is to examine options

9
00:00:26.956 --> 00:00:30.667
for reminders, not to change an individual's eligibility or

10
00:00:30.689 --> 00:00:34.044
the appointment rules. The people responsible for those matters

11
00:00:34.067 --> 00:00:35.711
remain responsible for them.

12
00:00:36.292 --> 00:00:39.092
Your own role may be to prepare a question,

13
00:00:39.314 --> 00:00:43.314
provide information, review a draft, coordinate input, or make

14
00:00:43.337 --> 00:00:47.226
a recommendation. A useful analysis makes those contributions visible

15
00:00:47.248 --> 00:00:50.226
without implying that one person holds every responsibility.

16
00:00:51.459 --> 00:00:54.214
Look for the sources that actually govern the work.

17
00:00:54.903 --> 00:00:58.659
These might include applicable law, current agency policy, service

18
00:00:58.681 --> 00:01:03.103
requirements, delegated procedures or a contract. A learning example,

19
00:01:03.459 --> 00:01:06.326
a summary or a proposed improvement is not automatically

20
00:01:06.348 --> 00:01:07.548
a governing requirement.

21
00:01:08.314 --> 00:01:12.292
The published DHS Equity Policy and the official Equity

22
00:01:12.314 --> 00:01:15.692
Analysis Toolkit are available from the existing toolkit and

23
00:01:15.714 --> 00:01:19.492
policy pages. Confirm the current policy, instructions and local

24
00:01:19.514 --> 00:01:22.181
review process for the decision you are working on.

25
00:01:22.203 --> 00:01:25.848
Where a required full analysis applies, a brief pause

26
00:01:25.870 --> 00:01:27.070
does not replace it.

27
00:01:28.848 --> 00:01:31.803
Do not settle a question of legal or policy

28
00:01:31.826 --> 00:01:36.292
interpretation simply because a source seems relevant. Record what

29
00:01:36.314 --> 00:01:39.603
you found, where you found it, what remains uncertain

30
00:01:39.959 --> 00:01:42.781
and the office that can interpret or confirm it.

31
00:01:43.048 --> 00:01:45.826
Separate a requirement that is verified from one that

32
00:01:45.848 --> 00:01:46.892
still needs review.

33
00:01:47.947 --> 00:01:51.169
Some parts of a proposal may be required; others

34
00:01:51.191 --> 00:01:54.302
may be choices. In the reminder example, the team

35
00:01:54.324 --> 00:01:57.947
should confirm what information must be communicated, whether a

36
00:01:57.969 --> 00:02:01.524
particular method is required, what consent or privacy rules

37
00:02:01.547 --> 00:02:04.769
apply and who is responsible for approving any change.

38
00:02:05.470 --> 00:02:09.181
Until the responsible people confirm those points, they are

39
00:02:09.203 --> 00:02:12.670
questions, not facts. There may be more than one

40
00:02:12.692 --> 00:02:15.892
way to meet a requirement. Ask which options can

41
00:02:15.914 --> 00:02:18.870
still be considered rather than assuming that a constraint

42
00:02:18.892 --> 00:02:20.826
makes every other choice impossible.

43
00:02:21.671 --> 00:02:24.982
The same distinction matters in a hiring process, a

44
00:02:25.004 --> 00:02:28.560
contract or a notice. Preserve binding requirements, and keep

45
00:02:28.582 --> 00:02:31.716
any proposed change clearly identified as a proposal until

46
00:02:31.738 --> 00:02:33.427
the appropriate decision is made.

47
00:02:34.793 --> 00:02:38.060
Identify roles rather than putting one person in charge

48
00:02:38.082 --> 00:02:41.349
of everything. Who owns the work? Who understands the

49
00:02:41.371 --> 00:02:45.771
governing requirements? Who can arrange meaningful participation? Who will

50
00:02:45.793 --> 00:02:49.993
review accessibility, privacy or communications when those subjects arise?

51
00:02:50.638 --> 00:02:51.993
Who can make the final decision?

52
00:02:52.893 --> 00:02:57.338
Formal processes, including those for civil rights, Tribal consultation,

53
00:02:57.849 --> 00:03:01.160
labor relations or other matters when applicable, remain in

54
00:03:01.182 --> 00:03:04.804
place. An equity analysis can inform them; it does

55
00:03:04.827 --> 00:03:08.316
not replace them. Ask the responsible office which processes

56
00:03:08.338 --> 00:03:11.293
apply rather than assuming they all apply to every

57
00:03:11.316 --> 00:03:11.738
example.

58
00:03:12.327 --> 00:03:15.571
The requirements crosswalk can help you keep the source,

59
00:03:15.971 --> 00:03:18.349
the work it affects, the evidence and the reviewer

60
00:03:18.371 --> 00:03:22.838
together. Its notes support preparation; completing a worksheet is

61
00:03:22.860 --> 00:03:23.993
not itself an approval.

62
00:03:25.223 --> 00:03:28.134
In the activity below, consider what to do when

63
00:03:28.157 --> 00:03:31.068
the reminder team is unsure whether a text-only approach

64
00:03:31.090 --> 00:03:35.890
meets the applicable requirements. Select a response, then read

65
00:03:35.912 --> 00:03:38.846
the feedback and compare the reasoning. You may revisit

66
00:03:38.868 --> 00:03:39.534
your choice.

67
00:03:40.103 --> 00:03:43.792
For practice, use general information. Do not include a

68
00:03:43.814 --> 00:03:48.170
person's appointment details, health information or other confidential records.

69
00:03:49.492 --> 00:03:53.848
For your own work example, identify one governing source,

70
00:03:54.381 --> 00:03:57.670
one part of the decision that remains open and

71
00:03:57.692 --> 00:04:01.337
one question that needs a responsible review. If you

72
00:04:01.359 --> 00:04:03.492
do not know a source or a role, it

73
00:04:03.514 --> 00:04:06.092
is useful to write that down as unknown.

74
00:04:06.714 --> 00:04:10.292
Next, we will consider whose experience can help answer

75
00:04:10.314 --> 00:04:14.226
the decision question, what existing evidence can show and

76
00:04:14.248 --> 00:04:15.714
what still needs to be learned.
